Chapter three: showing the knowledge of all bases.
Through the perfection of wisdom, wherever the hero acts,
They completely transcend the three realms, yet do not enter liberation;
Although afflictions are cleared away, they display birth;
Although without aging, sickness, and death, they display passing away.

Desiring honor and desiring gain,
With a mind that longs to view external objects, they become intimate with households;
Having forsaken the Dharma, they will engage in non-Dharma activities;
Having discarded the path, going on a wrong path—this is the work of Māra.
